## Step 3 — why the guard did not save it

$ read services/gateway/src/orb/live/instruction/instruction-budget.ts
-> INSTRUCTION_TOTAL_BYTE_BUDGET = 30_720
-> DROP_ORDER  = ['bootstrap','history','specialist']
-> PRESERVED   = ['scaffold','override']
-> contract: "if the preserved-only assembly still exceeds the budget the
   over-budget text is returned as-is (failing loudly via totalBytesAfter >
   budget for the caller to log)"

$ read services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts:7871-7920
-> logs stillOverBudget then SENDS ANYWAY (fail-open), console.warn only.

Both live dumps already contained "[bootstrap context omitted...]" => the guard
had already trimmed everything it is allowed to. Confirms it cannot rescue this.

